A||||48||Eric||Girls and Street Racing||||1||
Z||000000||Eric||06-07-2001||09:22 PM||||I was just driving up, and then down, my new favorite racing street.  To my good fortune, I pulled out right behind a VTEC Integra driven by a cute blone about 20 years old.  Well I don't know what her deal was, but I tried everything to get her to race me and she wouldn't.  I reved my engine, passed her, slowed down, and reved my engine again. But, no matter how hard I tried, I couldn't get her to so much as look up to see what the hell was going on.  There were even two guys on crotch rockets in the same group of traffic (they thought I was trying to race them  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  So what's the deal?  Doesn't she know that she's driving a fast car?  I've seen chicks in Vettes turn down races to Civics and other rice burners.  Gawd, they really wouldn't even have to try.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||grinthock||06-07-2001||09:31 PM||||Dude, Some people are just NOT INTO STREET RACING... <P>1)  It's illegal<P>2)  It's DANGEROUS<P>3)  You have no right driving like a moron around someone who doesn't want it.<P>4)  Keep it on the track - That's where racing is meant to be....  Or some back dirt road.  But if after one light the person doesn't want to race... Back off.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Urchin||06-07-2001||09:32 PM||||There are girls out there who are more than willing to race, trust me.  I had a girl in an olds cutlas try to race me from the merge lane.  I beat her, and she graciously gave me the one finger salute out the window  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I also have a couple of female friends who won't back down from a race either.  Kinda funny<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature2_3.jpg">   <P>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroLisa||06-07-2001||09:47 PM||||So Eric, just cause one girl does something, you assume we are all the same? I swear...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Umm I can imagine that she or her parents bought the car because it's a nice car, not because she wanted to take it and race some punks at a stoplight. She was probably trying to contain her laughter at you revving your engine anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87 Pegasus||06-07-2001||09:51 PM||||HA!!!!!!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Friends don't let friends drive Corvettes!!||||reg||10
Z||000005||banditbalz||06-07-2001||10:42 PM||||My Fiance, Becky, is 21 yrs and just loves to race. She has a '91 Cavalier RS with a strong 3.1 Just 10 minutes ago she was asking me if i wanted to run her at the dragstrip this weekend... i may just get my butt kicked!<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/launch_3.jpg">  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/banditbalz/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/banditbalz/</A> <P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||12
Z||000006||Slammed Fiero||06-07-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by grinthock:<BR><B>Dude, Some people are just NOT INTO STREET RACING... <P>1)  It's illegal<P>2)  It's DANGEROUS<P>3)  You have no right driving like a moron around someone who doesn't want it.<P>4)  Keep it on the track - That's where racing is meant to be....  Or some back dirt road.  But if after one light the person doesn't want to race... Back off.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hahahah of all people to post this one!!!!!!<P>JM <P>||||reg||1
Z||000007||Eric||06-07-2001||11:40 PM||||About three weeks ago or so, I posted a racing story about how I beat up on some girl in a gold Celica GTS.  So as not to contradict myself, I'll try and make my point clear to the rest of you.  I would expect anyone of any sex to at least give me a head shake or a race if I try that hard to draw attention to myself.  That is your duty if you drive a fast car, or in this case, a moderatly fast car.  Maybe she was having a rough day or was bummed about going to work.  The point is, I see so many girls in fast cars turn down races by just ignoring the guy in the other car.  It's wrong!  Drive the freaking base model if you don't want attention.<P>Grinthock, this road is huge.  I'm not running 100mph either.  You guys gotta just chill about street racing.  Okay that means no more flames.||||reg||1
Z||000008||saleenfiero||06-07-2001||11:47 PM||||Not putting all girls in one category, but the ones arounf my town, aged 16-25 drive like crazy, not race per say, but scream downthe road and crazy speeds.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Steve Normington||06-07-2001||11:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B>I would expect anyone of any sex to at least give me a head shake or a race if I try that hard to draw attention to myself.  That is your duty if you drive a fast car, or in this case, a moderatly fast car.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sorry, I have to disagree, just cause someone is driving a fast car doesn't mean that they have a "duty" to acknowledge you. Maybe they think you're some punk kid and they don't want to encourage your behaviour by paying attention to you.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Black88GT||06-08-2001||01:40 AM||||I'm with Eric on this one.  I have seen girls with insanely fast cars driving them in the far right lane at 60 mph.  It's just the way it is I guess.<P>Street racing is only dangerous if the people racing don't know what they are doing.  If you have a straight open road and 2 knowledgable racers lined up at a light, it's not dangerous.  <P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||grinthock||06-08-2001||06:48 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B> hahahah of all people to post this one!!!!!!<P>JM <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>hehehe.. I never said I practice what I preech!  <P><BR>I agreet wtih you on that 88GT, if it's safe!<P>FieroHeather races ricers in her parents 3.8 V6 Family Van and kicks their butts, it's hilarious!<BR><p>[This message has been edited by grinthock (edited 06-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000012||LZeitgeist||06-08-2001||06:54 AM||||I'm siding with Steve on this one - I don't have a 'duty' to you or anyone else, no matter *what* car I drive. <P>If you're looking for attention, look elsewhere - you won't get it from me. <P>If I choose to drive a Viper at 5MPH under the posted speed limit, that's my choice. It's got nothing to do with what anybody else is driving. <P>A 'duty'... that's the goofiest thing I've read on the Internet all week.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||06-08-2001||08:27 AM||||come down here... my new wife will wax the floor with ya in her little miata and tell EVERYONE "you got beat by a GIRL" heheh she likes rubbing that in peoples face..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats another reason i married her! ||||reg||1
Z||000014||AusFiero||06-08-2001||09:01 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>come down here... my new wife will wax the floor with ya in her little miata and tell EVERYONE "you got beat by a GIRL" heheh she likes rubbing that in peoples face..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> thats another reason i married her! </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You married her cause she has a Miata? Or because she likes rubbing something in ya face?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
Z||000015||Predator||06-08-2001||10:10 AM||||To each his/her own. It does not matter weather you are a woman or a man. If someone does not want to race just back off and leave them alone. I would have just ignored you if you had pulled that with me as well. I don't street race, and my car is fairly fast. I have seen to many accidents that way around here and was in a really bad one when I was a teenager. I learned the hard way. If you want to race take it to a track. Fiero's are rare enough around here, and nice ones are even harder to find. I won't take a chance on wrecking my car, because someone has  a lead foot, and can't keep it under control. I am not against a little fun. Every now and then the opportunity is there to goose it, and play a little, but I don't agree with a serious race on the street. That will get you or someone innocent killed. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||06-08-2001||10:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by xxxxxxxxx:<BR><B>I'm with Eric on this one...<P>Street racing is only dangerous if the people racing don't know what they are doing.  If you have a straight open road and 2 knowledgable racers lined up at a light, it's not dangerous.  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow...You guys amaze me. I have a "duty" to acknowledge your attempt to draw me into an illegal race? Street racing isn't dangerous?<P>...I wonder if the sh!thead that killed my friend felt the same way. Course, I'd have to hold a sayance to find out. <P>My friend was driving to work on the highway, late at night (he worked odd shifts). The road was empty, basically. 2 other guys were racing (supercharged Mustang vs. Corvette) up the highway, and came up on him at what looked to be well over 120mph. He had been in the left lane for some reason, and went to move over to let them pass, but their closing speeds were too great. The Vette was in the left lane, and the Mustang was in the right. The Mustang apparently lost control when my friend changed lanes, and clipped the Vette. All 3 went off the road, the Mustang into my friend's car. the Vette rolld a couple times, but the driver was OK. The Mustang ram-rodded my friend's car into an overpass embankment. The Mustang driver was killed instantly, and my friend died the next day. <P>Oh, sure "it can't happen to me" "I know what I'm doing". I've heard it all. <BR>He's not the only person I've known to die this way, and this is a small town. <P>If you street race, you are ignorant, irresponsible, and criminally neglegent. No matter how well you "think" you know what you're doing. Many street racers become the definition of "social darwinism", killing themselves (and others) in their ignorance. <P>Take it to the track. If not for yourself, for everyone else. <BR>Have a nice day.<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Slammed Fiero||06-08-2001||11:05 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Steve Normington:<BR><B> Sorry, I have to disagree, just cause someone is driving a fast car doesn't mean that they have a "duty" to acknowledge you. Maybe they think you're some punk kid and they don't want to encourage your behaviour by paying attention to you.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have to agree with this , We have a 94 911 RSR , every kid in the country tries to race it, with every car imagineable, my dad doesn't even bother, nor does he acknowledge goofs who rev their motor up and ride his ass in a cheezy attempt to street race. People get the false impression that street racing makes them a good driver. Too many variables in street racing to be an accurate measure of a cars performance. If you street race on a busy street it's more a case of playing who's a bigger dumbass and will risk lives other than their own. <P>We usually go out to an abandoned road on the outskirts of the city in the middle of no where. Keep it out of town , keep it away from crowds. <P>I'm by no means innocent of this , but thereis a time and place for everything. You wanna race go out to an autocross/ Drag strip , or a track. Lets see how good you really are. <P><BR><P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1607505&a=12259132&p=48230089&Sequence=0&res=high">     <BR>Jonathan McCreery<BR>86 GT 4spd<BR>Koni's , Coilovers, Big Bars , 17" Trmotorsports Typhoons , 11.25" vented discs, Wilwood 4 Piston Calipers , Pirelli P Zero's, Short Shift, No cat , Cold air induction , Geni Stainless tips, White face gauges , Momo shift , momo pedals..Autocrossed , Tracked , abused.||||reg||1
Z||000018||FieroLisa||06-08-2001||11:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>  If you street race on a busy street it's more a case of playing who's a bigger dumbass and will risk lives other than their own.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmmmmmmmmmm I seem to remember someone racing at every single light in the middle of town in their dad's wagon.........   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||LZeitgeist||06-08-2001||11:55 AM||||Uh, oh....<P><BR>BUS-TED!!!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000020||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||12:06 PM||||My friends and I used to go to Philly every friday / saturday night to go race his 92 Celica GT.<BR>One time we were following the cars, and he decided to get out and put his jacket on. Then we pulled back into the line.<BR>We were making a left and out of nowhere this 3000GT slammed into a Celebrety. 5 people were inside the Celebrety. One person somehow was tossed out of the back window. One out the front windshield. 2 people survived.<BR>The people in the 3000GT - the guy driving severed his foot at the ankle. The dashboard came down when he hit the pole on his final spin. The girl with him broke 3 ribs and punctured a lung. <BR>Now everytime I think about that night, I think "what if"...<BR>You see, that Celebrety was the next car behind us before we pulled over. So logical thinking, if he wasn't cold, that would have been me....||||reg||1
Z||000021||Black88GT||06-08-2001||12:34 PM||||.<p>[This message has been edited by Black88GT (edited 06-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Black88GT||06-08-2001||12:34 PM||||It seems most people that complain about street racing are those with slow cars.<P>I would like to see some of you in a brand new Z06 turn down a street race from some ricer Civic.  Yeah sure, take all those "ignorant, irresponsible" B.S. values and toss them out the window because you would be burning rubber with the Civic.||||reg||1
Z||000023||TRiAD||06-08-2001||12:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>It seems most people that complain about street racing are those with slow cars.<P>...take all those "ignorant, irresponsible" B.S. values and toss them out the window because you would be burning rubber with the Civic.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow. I'm normally not like this, but your ignorance seems to know no bounds. <BR>I own a company that has sold aftermarket bolt-ons for 8 years, and has been brokering Exotic sales for the last year. I have had occasion to drive MANY cars faster than I'm sure you can imagine. Diablo 6.0, 911 Turbo, Ferraris, Lotus, Lingenfelter Vettes, Callaway Twin Turbos, and one F50 (at a track day with one of my clients).<BR>I can honestly say, even when I drove a new 911 Turbo from Chicago to Memphis, that street racing is not a temptation. <BR>To be honest, I have driven fast on the street, and have raced on the street, when I was much younger, and even more ignorant. -Nothing like seeing people die to change your outlook. <BR>Unfortunately, you seem determined to learn from your own mistakes, and not the mistakes of others, so, so be it. I just hope you only hurt yourself, and no one else, if you must hurt someone to learn. <BR>Those <I>"ignorant, irresponsible" B.S. values</I> will be yours somedat too. Maybe after you kill someone, maybe when you have kids of your own, but someday. <BR>Keep your ignorance to yourself, and simply enjoy the other info you can get here...many of us do not want to hear of your maladjusted misadventures. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000024||The Fieromaster||06-08-2001||01:16 PM||||I am not agreeing or disagreeing with the way people race... I believe if you do it there are certain places that its just STUPID (busy roads and what not) although I am not saying i havent done that.  I look back on a rac i had in my Eclipse GSX vs. a turbo Honda... 130mph+ on a highway during rush hour in the "3rd" lane!  Ok that was dumb!!  We have a local place called the "snakes crossing" where everyone goes to race (undeveloped idustrial zone).  The name is derived from the Mustang boys that take everyone there to challenge them... Where are the turbo Fiero's when you can use em?  But as for girls... some arent as IN to street racing.. Even some of the chicks here who drive "riived out" cars just dont care how fast it is just that it LOOKS good!  Then there are the 2 or 3 chicks here with 99 Cobra's and there like MAD racers!  Oh and ungodly HOT!  Most of the guys here will race but if they know your car is faster they deliberatly drive in the opposite direction on the "main crusie" roads here!  That annoys me.. the talk crap but do nothing!<BR>But remember its not just street racing.. the most important person in my pathetic (lol) life was taken from me a year ago by a 82 year old blind (ok calming down - no cusin) lady... The worst part is she said "I saw him and thought i had enough time" So bad judgment or what ever youi rack that up is as bad!  <BR>Triad im so sorry to hear about your loss i feel your pain!<BR>But i guess if racing on the street is straigh stupidity then call me stupid because i dunno it just is in my blood...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.askfelons.com/fieromaster/fieromastergif1.gif">   <BR>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000<BR>1985 GT ~Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)<BR>1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX (AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000||||reg||1
Z||000025||DJRice||06-08-2001||01:39 PM||||Up in Jacksonville, the old international airport on the north side of town was a popular place to hold weekend drag races.  An abandoned runway seemed like a nice place to race...right up to the point where a tie rod broke on a Mustang GT at triple digit speeds and a bystander was injured and his child was killed when the car tumbled into the onlookers.<P>Even undeveloped industrial zones arent necessarily safe places to race.....  <P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/djr_signature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000026||DecadenceR||06-08-2001||01:43 PM||||Although I've seen what I've seen I still race occasionally.<BR>Like as some of the people from my area can tell you, Route 9 late at night can be pretty empty.<BR>Will you see me driving 90mph at 5pm? Hells no.<BR>but if it's late at night and I can see a clear open road I do.<BR>My funniest race ever was against a Viper 3am on Rt9. I knew i was gonna lose, but it was just for fun. I waved to the guy as he passed me. Point being at 3am, where we were, you can see down 2, 3 lights and you can tell if there's going to be a problem.<BR>Or we can take it out on the freeway - I95 is almost always open and plenty of room to move.||||reg||1
Z||000027||Steve Normington||06-08-2001||03:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DJRice:<BR><B>Up in Jacksonville, the old international airport on the north side of town was a popular place to hold weekend drag races.  An abandoned runway seemed like a nice place to race...right up to the point where a tie rod broke on a Mustang GT at triple digit speeds and a bystander was injured and his child was killed when the car tumbled into the onlookers.<P>Even undeveloped industrial zones arent necessarily safe places to race.....  <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>At least they had a chioce to be there.||||reg||1
Z||000028||FieroHeather||06-08-2001||04:23 PM||||My favourite strip to beat people off of the line at lights has got to be in Guelph on Woodlawn Rd.  There are over 10 stop lights, and if you time the speed just right, you can make it through 6 of them no problem.  In my parents van, it is funny to beat family wagons, ricers and even drivers who dont know how to drive vets!  (SlammedFiero's sleeper wagon not included)  But if the situation is unsafe, I immedately STOP racing, and drive normal.  I dont go looking for races, nor do I encourage it from those beside me at lights.<P>As from a female perspective, street racing is exciting, even if you are a passenger... but being safe about it all is the key to the fun.<P>Have a good weekend all!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000029||Fiero Sam||06-08-2001||05:42 PM||||Believe it or not,I always stick to the speed limit.I never agree with what's posted,I always feel I could drive faster and still be safe and responsible.Sometimes I feel like I am the only one who drives the speed limit.I got in a race one time.I got up to 75(the speed limit was 55) and just didn't want to go any faster,so I slowed up(hardly a race at 75,I know).Right around the corner was a cop!<BR>I can't remember if the other guy got a ticket or not(I hope so) but I didn't.<BR>I'm too old for racing.||||reg||1
Z||000030||Tina||06-08-2001||07:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Eric:<BR><B> I've seen chicks in Vettes turn down races to Civics and other rice burners.  Gawd, they really wouldn't even have to try.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Exactly my point.<BR>Why bother,<BR>when you know the outcome before you even let the clutch up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Don't get me wrong, I'am not one that never races.<BR>But when I do,<BR>I rather choose my battles. <BR>More fun that way.<BR>Not necessarily safe but safer.<P>Tina<P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Eric||06-08-2001||07:57 PM||||I almost got to race a woman driving a C5 convertable today.  Of course she probably wouldn't have tried me anyway.  Unfortunatly there was too much traffic and we didn't get an opportunity to line up against eachother.  <P>I don't know what you guys think about me, but I don't race to triple digit speeds.  Most of my races are only to the speed limit and the others are only a few miles per hour over.  I don't continue racing, if the car is equally matched, beyond the point where I feel comfortable.  I'm sorry for those of you who have lost friends, but don't try to compare me with the people who were going 120 and killed them.  NO FLAMES PLEASE!<P>If anyone can still respond to the original topic, please do so.||||reg||1
Z||000032||Sleeper||06-08-2001||08:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Black88GT:<BR><B>Street racing is only dangerous if the people racing don't know what they are doing.  If you have a straight open road and 2 knowledgable racers lined up at a light, it's not dangerous.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>i agree. in my opinion, what kills street racing out here in south bay are 2 groups of ppl:<P>dudes with new mustangs. they don't want their pride hurt by getting beat by a import so intead of racing they TRY and showoff by doing donuts in the middle of the street ppl are racing on. then they wonder what happened when someone racing hits them or they lose control in the spin and hit a telephone  pole...<P>4 door honda guys. they race with like 4 or 5 ppl in the car, "hey bros come jump in the car and watch me smoke this camaro". usually these are first time racers too, they race til like 100mph and hit a bump, lose control, hit the curb or flip, and kill 1 or more of his buddies or his girlfriend.<P><P>------------------<BR>85 GT Auto<BR>17" Racing Hart C5 wheels wrapped with Kumho Ecsta Supra 712 tires, Intrax lowering springs, KYB shocks, KYB-GR2 struts, West Coast Fiero Strut Tower Bar, West Coast Fiero Cold-Air Intake w/ HKS Super Flow filter, J.E.T. super chip and MSD Blaster Coil.||||reg||1
Z||000033||grinthock||06-08-2001||08:23 PM||||Well come to think of it, whenever I race on the street it's always<P>1)  And empty road, or NOTHING ahead and NOTHING ahead that could jump out<P>2)  NOT raining, snowing or otherwise<P>3)  I race up to the speed limit (or maybe 10 over) then cut it out, I love these idiots who just GUN IT up to 60mph then at the next light laugh, I feel like saying, Dude, I killed you to 300' that's what matters right here, not who can get to 2x the speed limit!||||reg||1
Z||000034||Eric||06-08-2001||08:39 PM||||I think most people race like you and I, grinthock.  I'll leave the high speed stuff for the track, but I still love taking low speed corners sideways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Oh boy, I just opened up a whole new can of worms.||||reg||1
Z||000035||Her86GT||06-08-2001||08:48 PM||||Personally, I think the best part about a race in the city is who gets off the line first.  Once up to speed, I feel the glory!!!  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Her86GT.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000036||ArchMagi||06-08-2001||10:25 PM||||I was comming home one night around 1am and I stopped at one of the longest lights in town, only to find 2 blonds in a brand new sunfire, yelling and screaming, honking the horn! I waved and said Hi.<P>I Won  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000037||Philphine||06-08-2001||11:38 PM||||i have to tell you. if you did that around me, you probaly wouldn't want my attention. i'd be about ready to jump out of the car and hit you. i hate that as much as i hate tailgaters.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> gettin' angry just thinking about it.<P>if a person dosen't want to race, go away.||||reg||1
Z||000038||fyerstarter||06-09-2001||12:01 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sleeper:<BR><B> <BR>i agree. in my opinion, what kills street racing out here in south bay are 2 groups of ppl:<P>dudes with new mustangs. they don't want their pride hurt by getting beat by a import so intead of racing they TRY and showoff by doing donuts in the middle of the street ppl are racing on. then they wonder what happened when someone racing hits them or they lose control in the spin and hit a telephone  pole...<P>4 door honda guys. they race with like 4 or 5 ppl in the car, "hey bros come jump in the car and watch me smoke this camaro". usually these are first time racers too, they race til like 100mph and hit a bump, lose control, hit the curb or flip, and kill 1 or more of his buddies or his girlfriend.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>...and then there is the third type. You. The "responsible" racer. In places where there are stop lights the speed limit is never more than 45 mph. There is no way you can tell me that you "race" to 45 and then cut it off. That's not even out of second gear. So here you are haulin ass down the street when one of the mustang boys decides to do a donut in the street, or rice boy and his friends hits a burm in the opposite lane and comes flying in front of you, or the little old blind lady at the cross walk thinks the red hand looks like the green guy and decides to start walking across.....<P>....and you're too busy paying attention to racing and going to fast for it to make a difference anyway<P><BR>You ever notice the people who are racing at stop lights? It's never people with fast cars. It's a bunch of economy or mild performance cars trying to pretend they are race cars. If anyone pulls up next to me and starts revving like an idiot in the middle of traffic I just roll down the window and say "wanna race?"...ok, then follow me. And take em out to the strawberry fields where there are some nice abandoned roads suitable for racing. Needless to say most just laugh and all of a sudden "have to be somewhere" or just burn out and make a quick left to go harass the next driver. Because they know in a real race their car isn't fast. But in a street race a Honda Civic can beat a Viper (sure it may be because there was traffic in front of the Vipers lane) but they won't tell their friends that. <P>You want a good laugh? Visit <A HREF="http://www.speedmagazine.com/stories/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.speedmagazine.com/stories/</A>  ,if you believe that street racing is any kind of test of performance or skill then you'll believe half the crap here   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 06-09-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000039||Black88GT||06-09-2001||12:09 AM||||Haha.  I like how when people disagree with others they say "keep it to yourself".  In other words "I am always right and I don't like when people disagree with me".<P>I have seen accidents during street races.  I have seen people die (not during street races though).  I will always street race, however the older I get the more I will win (more money, faster car).  <P>That "why bother" stuff is funny too.  Just because you have a vette doesn't mean you can pull 13s in the Qtr.  Most don't even know how to drive them.  I have seen CRX's beat vette's on more then when occasion.  Yeah, we all know the Vette is technically faster, but the driver can make the difference against a 14 second CRX. <P>Cya at the light.... <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000040||Sleeper||06-09-2001||12:17 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fyerstarter:<BR><B>  ...and then there is the third type. You. The "responsible" racer. In places where there are stop lights the speed limit is never more than 45 mph. There is no way you can tell me that you "race" to 45 and then cut it off. That's not even out of second gear. So here you are haulin ass down the street when one of the mustang boys decides to do a donut in the street, or rice boy and his friends hits a burm in the opposite lane and comes flying in front of you, or the little old blind lady at the cross walk thinks the red hand looks like the green guy and decides to start walking across.....<P>....and you're too busy paying attention to racing and going to fast for it to make a difference anyway<P>[This message has been edited by fyerstarter (edited 06-09-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>i don't race, i watch...why would i want to race a nice import with nos that will smoke my fairly stock auto GT. nice try ,tell me another story about the "granny that crossed the road".  <P>my racing begins whenever i get off my ass and buy a 3.8<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000041||DaRkLoRD||06-09-2001||01:04 AM||||I've officially raced 2 cars, a civic and a neon. I have no idea what the engines were in them, but they were looking at me and revving their engines, so I figured why not. in both cases, we were on a 4-lane highway, no one in front of us, no cops around, and definitely no kids. In the first one, a guy in a black civic who's only mod seemed to be a big exhaust tip, was revving the heck out of his engine at a stoplight.. so I figured, why not. when the light turned greenm I stepped on it, not even at full throttle, and toasted him in about 2 seconds.. I went up to about 60kph (50 zone.. was near a town) and then let off the gas. shortly afterwards, he passed me and also slowed down.. end of story.. on the way out of town, about an hour later, a middle aged guy in a new red neon did the same thing!! I was sitting at the same set of lights, going the other way, and I heard an engine revving. looked over and there was a middle aged guy looking at me.... anyway, I figured it might be a 6cyl, so I thought I'd see what it could do.. I let him have about half a second's head start, and then stomped on it... and spun the tires... lost almost another second... but then I still caught up to him before we hit 100! at that point we were on the highway, so I set the cruise at 95kph, and kept driving. The funny part about this story, is that I was at a park eating lunch after I got back into town, and the same red neon pulled in right beside me, and sat at the table next to me...???<BR>I felt like asking if he wanted to see who could eat lunch faster too.......  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>anyway, sorry I didn't have anything to post on the original topic.. but I just felt offering my 2 cents about street racing.<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
Z||000042||fyerstarter||06-09-2001||02:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sleeper:<BR><B> <BR>i don't race, i watch...why would i want to race a nice import with nos that will smoke my fairly stock auto GT. nice try ,tell me another story about the "granny that crossed the road".  <P>my racing begins whenever i get off my ass and buy a 3.8</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yeah me too. I have an 87 GT with some mods but it's not very fast. Most of our cars are not. If you tell yourself that a Fiero is a fast care you're kidding yourself. Now throw a Northstar or a 3.8 in there and that's a different story. To me it's pretty comical seeing these people in their neons, and civics, and nissan maximas...AND FIEROS racing each other like they are high performance machines, when they would be lucky to break into the 15's with those cars. I mean if someone wants to race me I'll race em, out on some deserted road somewhere just for fun. But not in the middle of town where people are just trying to take care of their ****  and get home without getting killed by somebody who thinks their bottom line econobox is a race car.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000043||TRiAD||06-09-2001||06:15 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>...I felt like asking if he wanted to see who could eat lunch faster too.......   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>BWaaaahhhaaaahahahahahaha!<BR>That's awesome!<BR><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||10
Z||000044||rogergarrison||06-09-2001||07:45 AM||||I do my 'street racing' on the interstates and when traffic is non existant or sparse. My fav is out in the country, no one else around but me, so no ones in danger but me and my car. BTW I did race a ZO6 and they are fast, we played back n forth on I-270 for several miles. I dont get stomped often, but he totally smoked me.<P>As for the girls issue, almost all I know drive with the pedal all the way down, whether its the brake or gas. Theres no inbetween. (after all, there the 'go' and 'stop' buttons, right?)||||reg||1
Z||000045||DaRkLoRD||06-09-2001||05:16 PM||||Wait, I almost forgot about another "race".. I was behind a Talon TSi once, and we both stomped on it when we got the green light at an intersection. his turbo hadn't spooled up yet I guess, cause I had to hit the brakes.. he was in my way.. but later on he was still in front of me (long stretch of empty road, middle of the day) and he hit the gas.. remembering the performance before, I figured I could catch him.. I took it up to around 150kph, but he was pulling ahead so fast it was like I was standing still... <P>but *usually* I stick to close to the speed limit.. hehe..<P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
